# 🐧 1. Linux Fundamentals

Before becoming a Linux Administrator, it's important to understand the basic concepts of Linux and build a proper lab environment.

---

## Lab Setup

Practice Linux inside a virtual environment before working on production servers.

Recommended options:

- Oracle VirtualBox
- VMware Workstation
- KVM

---

## Popular Linux Distributions

| Distribution | Purpose |
|--------------|----------|
| Ubuntu | Beginner Friendly |
| Debian | Stable Servers |
| RHEL | Enterprise Production |
| Rocky Linux | Free RHEL Alternative |
| AlmaLinux | Enterprise Linux |
| Kali Linux | Penetration Testing |

---

## Linux File System

Understanding the Linux directory structure is essential.

```
/
├── bin
├── boot
├── dev
├── etc
├── home
├── lib
├── media
├── mnt
├── opt
├── proc
├── root
├── run
├── srv
├── sys
├── tmp
├── usr
└── var
```

---

## Essential Commands

```
pwd
ls
cd
mkdir
rm
cp
mv
touch
cat
less
nano
vim
find
locate
grep
echo
history
clear
```

